cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated manuscript and the archived Zenodo release."
title: "R code for Hysteresis metrics reveal land-use-dependent stormflow constituent dynamics in tropical Afromontane catchments"
version: "1.0.0"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Tabo"
    given-names: "Zadoki"
  - family-names: "Jacobs"
    given-names: "Suzanne R."
  - family-names: "Breuer"
    given-names: "Lutz"

repository-code: "https://github.com/jluzt2022/mau-hysteresis-reproducibility"

abstract: >
  R code supporting the reproducibility of the manuscript
  "Hysteresis metrics reveal land-use-dependent stormflow constituent dynamics
  in tropical Afromontane catchments". The default public workflow reproduces
  publication-specific analyses, tables, and figures from processed and derived
  datasets archived separately in Zenodo. The original 10-minute monitoring
  workflow is retained for provenance but requires authorized access to the
  non-public source dataset.

keywords:
  - hysteresis
  - storm events
  - hydrochemistry
  - flushing
  - tropical catchments
  - Afromontane
  - reproducible research
  - R

license: MIT
